From 7d884755cebd8ec996c427011938ec3f3653a5be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:33:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 207/225] feat: reconstruct the full material at a ray traced
 hit - detail mapping, blend layer, per type parameters (decision 10)

RT_ProcessBestHit stopped at the four base record slots: albedo, normal, specular, emissive. A
detail mapped wall reflected as a flat wall, a blend layer material reflected as its first layer
only, and a vegetation / skin / glass / water hit reflected as plain Illum. This reads the extras
record report 05A's producer writes and rebuilds what Illum.cfx actually shades.

THE RAW UV. The traversal only kept the ATLAS coordinate of the albedo layer, and every extras
layer applies its own tiling to the raw uv BEFORE the wrap. So the winning triangle's fourth
texel is re-read at the hit (it also carries the material record index, which SBestHit does not)
and the raw uv is rebuilt from the three packed per vertex UVs. RT_ExtrasAtlasTC then wraps each
layer with its own tiling through the material's own offset and atlas scale, so an extras layer
lands on the same texel grid the albedo does.

%BLENDLAYER, Illum.cfx:507-533 / shadeLib.cfi:1039-1049. extras+1 points at an ABSOLUTE record
index holding a full second base record, so it decodes through the same lanes and the two results
are lerped by the mask: albedo, smoothness (from the blend normal slice's alpha, where the
producer put smoothness2Tex), BlendLayer2Specular as a scalar reflectance, and the tangent space
normal. blendFac is GetLayerBlendingValue verbatim - saturate(pow(vtxAlpha * mask.r *
(1 + BlendFactor), BlendFalloff)) - with vtxAlpha substituted by 1, because the triangle record
has no vertex colour lane (report 05A section 3). Applied before the detail map, as in Illum.

%DETAIL_MAPPING, Illum.cfx:548-559. ONE texture: Common.cfi:149 GetDetailTex samples .garb * 2 - 1,
so (g, a) is the tangent space normal, r the albedo delta and b the gloss delta, scaled by
detailScales.xxyz. The detail slice shares the atlas with the albedo, so it needs no separate sRGB
handling; the producer stores it raw, which is why the .garb swizzle is done here. The bump half
is multiplied by the same e_svoTI_RT_NormalsFading distance fade the base normal map gets, so a
distant detail mapped surface flattens as one surface. DetailGlossScale has no lane in the record
(report 05A gap 4) and uses the shader default 0.5.

THE HITMAT LANE, a sixth MRT. Each type needs a colour plus a scalar at the hit and there is no
spare lane: HITPOS.w is a full 24 bit integer since stage 2D, RAYDIR.xyz carries the VNDF weight
in its length since 4B, RAYDIR.w is the hit distance and the RT-pixel sentinel, RGB.w is the
reflecting pixel's depth, ALD is the normal and the emissive hue, and HITGI.w is the voxel AO that
multiplies the whole indirect diffuse. So ConeTracePS writes a half4 at SV_Target5 instead:
  .x   RT_PackHitMatCode - (code * 256 + param8 + 1), negated when the material has an extras
       record. Max 1792 and fp16 is exact to 2048, so the round trip is exact; the +1 makes the
       sign survive for code 0 and makes an unwritten pixel decode as "no material data".
  .yzw the one per type float3.
Resolved at the hit, per texel, from the shader each type is named after:
  0.25 vegetation  saturate(BackDiffuseMultiplier * translucencyMap) * TransmittanceColor
                   (Vegetation.cfx:503-512)
  2    human skin  exp((1 - saturate(translucencyMap * TranslucencyMultiplier)) * (-8, -40, -64))
                   (HumanSkin.cfx:295-298), plus SSSIndex in the 8 bit scalar
  3    glass       TintColor.rgb, plus TintCloudiness in the scalar (Glass.cfx:566-578)
  4    water       the fog colour attenuated by exp2(-density * depth) (Water.cfx:1116-1117), plus
                   ReflectionScale in the scalar; the sun specular multiplier (Water.cfx:632) is
                   folded into the reflectance lane, which is what scales the sun highlight
  0 / 5            nothing; a plain Illum or terrain hit is unchanged

The traversal is untouched. Its existing stipple test is ALREADY the stochastic transparency
decision 10 asks for - opacity * albedo alpha against the 2x2 screen stipple, so a pane at opacity
0.5 is seen through in half the phases and the stage 4B temporal filter resolves them - and its
back face rule already matches decision 10 (two sided for leaves, single sided for everything
else). Both are now documented in place with the v2 continuation ray and the vertex alpha gap.

Renderer: pRT_HITMAT_0, an R16G16B16A16F target the size of the other g-data targets, created and
destroyed with them under e_svoTI_RT_Active, bound at MRT slot 5 on ConeTracePass and at t39 on
ShadePass. With the feature off nothing is allocated and slot 5 is explicitly unbound, exactly as
slots 2-4 already are.

